; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Fractal Star
; CATEGORY: Fractals
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     recursion, star, fractal, repeat
; SUMMARY:  Draws a star with a smaller star at every point, and smaller stars on those.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   A five pointed star is drawn by turning 144 degrees at each tip.
;   At every tip a star one third as big is added, then smaller ones
;   on those, so the star sparkles all the way down.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Try different sizes and depths on the last line.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * the 144 degree turn that makes a star
;   * calling a procedure from inside REPEAT
;   * recursion with a depth counter
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Change 0.35 to 0.5 and watch the stars crowd together.
;   * Use depth 4. How many little stars are drawn now?
;   * Draw a fractal hexagon by turning 60 six times instead.
; ============================================================

; STAR draws a five pointed star. After each edge, before turning,
; the turtle sits on a tip, which is where the smaller star goes.
to star :size :depth
  if :depth = 0 [stop]
  repeat 5 [
    ; Set the color before every edge: the little stars change the pen
    ; color, and we want this edge in the color of its own depth.
    setpencolor item :depth [4 14 6 3]
    forward :size
    ; The small star is drawn here, then the turtle comes back to this
    ; same spot and heading, so the big star carries on unharmed.
    star :size * 0.35 :depth - 1
    right 144
  ]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [20 20 50]
setpensize 2
; A star with edges of 280 fits in a circle of radius 280 / 1.902.
; Start a little below the middle of the screen (the small stars need
; room at the top), walk up to the top tip, then face the tip that is
; two points along (heading 162), so the star ends up centered.
penup setxy 0 -25 setheading 0 forward 280 / 1.902 setheading 162 pendown
star 280 4
